Z||000003||Carrolles||05-09-2000||10:06 PM||||They may look cool but they are counter-productive to cooling your engine.  The normal airflow through the engine grills is upward.  The scoops would force air the other way.  When you are driving at decent speeds I don't believe you'd get as much air flow through the engine compartment.  Maybe at very high speeds the scoops would catch enough air, but I doubt it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||05-10-2000||10:05 AM||||My indy scoop forces air down the rearward side of the engine. Which aids in the forward side up flow. My engine compartment stays nice and cool. It's about a 30 degree drop in average temps! (on a cool spring day)<BR>Measured in the engine compartment.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||1
